PRODUCTNAME_PARSER — MASTER BUILD PROMPT
========================================

Role
----
You are a senior TypeScript/Node.js library architect specializing in:

- Local LLM inference
- Structured information extraction
- Function calling and tool calling
- Product catalog normalization
- Deterministic data pipelines
- Runtime schema validation
- Field-level confidence estimation
- Configurable domain-specific parsing
- Offline-first applications

Build the complete production-grade TypeScript/Node.js repository described below. Do not return only a conceptual architecture. Create the actual source files, configuration, tests, examples, README, and working HTML demo.

The repository name is:

productName_parser

The project must be suitable for the Git repository:

https://github.com/ammisaidkaidi/productName_parser.git

1. Scope
--------

The library is responsible only for product description parsing and normalization.

Do not implement:

- Semantic search
- Embeddings
- Vector databases
- pgvector
- BM25
- Ranking
- Recommendation
- Product similarity search

The core parser must work offline without OpenAI, cloud APIs, internet access, or external databases. A local LLM is optional and injectable.

2. Core objective
-----------------

Input:

ROBINET ARRET LAITON MF 1/2 SOMATHERM PRO REF RA12

Expected canonical output:

{
  "category": "plomberie",
  "subcategory": "robinet",
  "name": "robinet d'arrêt",
  "abbreviation": null,
  "collisage": null,
  "model": null,
  "brand": "Somatherm",
  "serie": "Pro",
  "quality": null,
  "madein": null,
  "material": "laiton",
  "dims": ["1/2"],
  "color": null,
  "ref": "RA12",
  "other": ["MF"]
}

Never invent unsupported information. If a value is not supported by the input or configured domain knowledge, return null for scalar fields and [] for array fields.

3. Canonical schema
-------------------

Implement a strongly typed TypeScript schema and a runtime Zod schema.

interface ParsedProduct {
  category: string | null;
  subcategory: string | null;
  name: string | null;
  abbreviation: string | null;
  collisage: string | null;
  model: string | null;
  brand: string | null;
  serie: string | null;
  quality: string | null;
  madein: string | null;
  material: string | null;
  dims: string[];
  color: string | null;
  ref: string | null;
  other: string[];
}

The architecture must remain extensible. Applications must be able to add configured fields without rewriting the parser pipeline or hard-coding the architecture around the initial fields.

Every final result must be runtime-validated. The LLM output must never be trusted directly.

4. Input preservation
---------------------

Always preserve:

- rawInput: the exact original description
- normalizedInput: the deterministic pre-normalized description

Normalization must never overwrite rawInput.

