Configuration editor requirements:

1. Categories & subcategories tab
   - Edit categories JSON.
   - Edit subcategories JSON.
   - Support aliases and category relationships.

2. Brands & series tab
   - Edit brands.
   - Edit brand aliases.
   - Edit series.
   - Edit series aliases.

3. Model rules tab
   - Edit model regex patterns.
   - Edit allowed model values.
   - Configure capture groups.

4. LLM field instructions tab
   - Select any property.
   - Edit field description.
   - Edit instructions line by line.
   - Edit examples line by line.
   - Save changes to the running parser.

The UI must call the actual parser/API. Do not use fake hard-coded output.

Implement demo API endpoints:

- GET /api/config
- POST /api/config
- POST /api/config/reset
- POST /api/parse

Saving configuration must validate the configuration and rebuild the active parser.

The server must:

- bind to 0.0.0.0
- serve demo/index.html
- support OPTIONS requests
- provide CORS headers suitable for the live preview
- return JSON errors
- support configurable PORT environment variable
- not require a cloud service

