18. Definition of done
----------------------

The project is complete only when:

- TypeScript compiles without errors.
- All tests pass.
- The parser returns schema-valid canonical data.
- Qwen is accessed only through the provider adapter.
- Function calling works through the generic registry.
- Taxonomy configuration is dynamic.
- Brands and series are hierarchical and configurable.
- Category/subcategory extraction uses the configured taxonomy first.
- Abbreviation and collisage fields work.
- Quality and madein fields work.
- Dimensions including 45deg and 45° work.
- PC product parsing works.
- Missing information becomes null/empty.
- Ambiguity triggers tools or unresolved values rather than guessing.
- Reference and dimensions remain separate.
- Normalization is deterministic and configurable.
- Raw and normalized inputs are preserved.
- Batch parsing works.
- Debug information is structured and contains no chain-of-thought.
- The HTML demo calls the actual parser/API.
- The configuration editor updates the running parser.
- The API server supports a configurable port and live preview access.
- No search, embedding, ranking, or recommendation functionality exists.
- The project can run locally without a cloud dependency.
- The final repository is committed and pushed to the configured remote.

Final instruction
-----------------

Build the actual working project. Prioritize:

Correctness
> Determinism
> Extensibility
> Low latency
> Developer experience

Do not silently add functionality outside product parsing and normalization.
